-260720-21bsr2: cross-platform candidate evidence may use an explicitly supplied suite root, but this task must not commit an unreleased curator-spec ref. Official released-suite pin provenance is audited by TASK-260720-1utsx8 after TASK-260720-25d05o.\nSolution-architecture audit 2026-07-20: scope and AC now keep candidate-suite validation out of the committed release pin. See outcome TASK-260720-3pemm6_release-boundary-plan.md; TASK-260720-1utsx8 alone advances the pin after TASK-260720-25d05o.","scope":"Own new cocoaskills test fixtures, end-to-end and process-level tests, and .github/workflows/ci.yml changes needed to select the operator-trusted accepted Go release family recorded in the protocol and Curator handoff evidence, family 1.25 in the currently accepted Curator implementation with Go 1.23 as the protocol floor only, and to run the exact rc.5 candidate suite without advancing the default committed curator-spec release pin. Real-fixture go-v1 build, cache, activation, launch, repair and rollback coverage runs on native macOS and native Windows runners. The ubuntu jobs keep running portable non-driver coverage such as models, CCJ-1, POSIX cache, locks and transactions, and shims, and must assert that the source-aware go-v1 path fails closed there rather than producing a green build. Cross-platform candidate qualification may accept an explicit immutable curator-spec revision or pre-materialized CURATOR_CONFORMANCE_ROOT as a non-default caller input, and must record its full manifest digest. Exercise project, global, hybrid, mixed script and build commands, and platform shims with real subprocesses. Use injected failures and fake toolchains only for negative paths. Linux go-v1 driver qualification is out of scope and stays with TASK-260728-1skseh and TASK-260728-1e6811. Do not change product semantics except narrowly scoped testability hooks routed to owning tasks; the released-suite pin belongs to TASK-260720-1utsx8 after TASK-260720-25d05o.","status":"backlog","title":"Add cross-platform Go build end-to-end tests"}
/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/curator/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260729-v5hqnv/TASK-260729-v5hqnv_after.jsonl:6:{"ac":"python -m pytest -v passes against the rc.5 candidate conformance root with no unexpected skips; python -m mypy passes in strict mode; python -m build and python -m twine check dist/* pass; git diff --check passes; and the native macOS and native Windows CI matrix with the real Go fixture is green across the supported Python matrix. The ubuntu jobs are green for portable non-driver coverage and assert the fail-closed source-aware path; Linux go-v1 driver success is neither required nor claimed. A task-scoped report records exact cocoaskills and curator-spec SHAs, the full rc.5 manifest digest sha256:b6f56aacc0e37dcc6692f73f641bff761e89b645adfe20a47a06d81c6fda204c, commands, logs, platform evidence, and a matrix mapping every STORY-260720-1uv5gi acceptance criterion plus every required rejection, lifecycle, cache, dry-run, rollback, status, launch, execution-policy identity, native-control-inventory and capability-evidence case to passing evidence. No conformance claim is emitted, no package-produced code runs during install verification, no committed release pin moves, and no release evidence is fabricated.","blockedBy":["TASK-260720-3pemm6","TASK-260720-akf5kh"],"blocks":["TASK-260720-1utsx8","TASK-260720-3pvihp","TASK-260720-2g7avf","TASK-260720-p7sdhg","TASK-260728-1ph8rs","TASK-260728-1j72zq","TASK-260728-2yxdo7","TASK-260728-3j60e3","TASK-260728-3ar1qp"],"description":"Perform the final clean integration verification for the independent Python schema 6 and go-v1 implementation against the rc.5 portable manager-worker-v1 contract, and attach reproducible evidence mapped to every story criterion and protocol vector cluster.","id":"TASK-260720-3s27te","name":"integrated-csk-v6-verification","notes":"Cross-story verification boundary from STORY-260720-21bsr2: candidate-suite evidence is not release evidence and must record the exact supplied suite digest without advancing a committed pin. The released-suite pin and no-skip CI audit is TASK-260720-1utsx8 after protocol release qualification.","scope":"Work from the landed dependency handoffs and the immutable curator-spec 1.0.0-rc.5 candidate conformance root supplied through CURATOR_CONFORMANCE_ROOT, whose manifest.json must hash to sha256:b6f56aacc0e37dcc6692f73f641bff761e89b645adfe20a47a06d81c6fda204c. This is a verification task, not a new design task. Run the repository-supported full test, strict typing, packaging metadata, cross-platform CI, and conformance commands from a clean task worktree. Native real-fixture go-v1 verification covers macOS and Windows; Linux stays explicitly deferred to TASK-260728-1skseh and TASK-260728-1e6811 and no Linux driver success may be claimed. Make only narrow integration corrections; route substantive defects to the owning task. Record that cocoaskills has no separate lint command unless one is added before execution, and run any declared lint gate that exists at that time.","status":"backlog","title":"Verify integrated csk schema v6 implementation"}
