/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/curator/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260729-v5hqnv/TASK-260729-v5hqnv_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--codex-_RUN-260729-769c54.log:1334:| Root | unpinned candidate suite | `CURATOR_CONFORMANCE_ROOT` whose `manifest.json` must hash to `sha256:b6f56aac…`, cross-checked against `release/1.0.0-rc.5.json` |
/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/curator/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260729-v5hqnv/TASK-260729-v5hqnv_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--codex-_RUN-260729-769c54.log:1532:{"ac":"The canonical go-v1 input requires policy.execution_policy = manager-worker-v1. CCJ-1 input bytes reproduce the shared 869-byte expected/build-driver/build-input.ccj.json and derive the shared cache key sha256:529370122ae11e2e961d5265b1a020e046bcd43165b2eb96b05e73a51187ac9b. Exact stored receipt bytes reproduce the shared 1120-byte expected/build-driver/receipt.ccj.json, contain no BOM, whitespace, or trailing newline, and derive the shared receipt hash sha256:919fbbad8e6ce95532219fd952c2309d0d7026f85209650508fd6834af4020cd. Both legacy identities from vectors/build-drivers.json cache_identity are required non-alias negatives with schema_valid false: legacy_rc4_without_execution_policy sha256:3fcd714a40e8918eb67dbd35d435875dcce6c9047da811a1fa26626e5e57be48 with no execution_policy, and reserved_hardened sha256:13736230d33ce59de7f7323dcd4cffd510655ad8dabd5ee9e8b6cb182ec70037 with execution_policy hardened-worker-v1; aliases is false and the three keys stay numerically distinct, so ignoring execution_policy can never produce the portable key. Readers reject duplicate keys, unsafe integers, noncanonical bytes, unknown fields, mismatched keys or input, missing or unknown execution_policy, wrong derived artifact paths, unsupported versions, and malformed identities. Marker v2 deterministically sorts roots, commands, dependencies, files, and builds; matches expected/build-driver/marker.json with schema_version 2, skill_schema_version 6, and a builds entry carrying driver go-v1 plus cache_key, receipt_sha256, artifact_path and artifact_sha256; requires build_source exactly when builds are active; and keeps valid marker v1 current for pre-v6 packages. Every golden is read from the caller-supplied rc.5 candidate root whose manifest.json hashes to sha256:b6f56aacc0e37dcc6692f73f641bff761e89b645adfe20a47a06d81c6fda204c, and the suite digest is recorded as non-release evidence. Focused pytest and strict mypy pass.","blockedBy":["TASK-260720-3c0ss2","TASK-260720-3j8pp5","TASK-260729-3nx97g"],"blocks":["TASK-260720-2jfnz6"],"description":"Implement portable logical build input including the rc.5-required execution_policy member, CCJ-1 cache keys, exact canonical receipt bytes and hashes, and install-marker v2 models while keeping physical csk cache paths implementation-specific.","id":"TASK-260720-2dnqw2","name":"canonical-build-metadata","notes":"","scope":"Own typed metadata modules under src/csk/builds, a dedicated install-marker model module, narrowly shared CCJ-1 support in src/csk/protocol_json.py, and focused tests. Model the complete go-v1 input including build source, root, command, source directory, native target, toolchain, and the fixed policy, whose required rc.5 common.schema.json goBuildPolicyV1 members are module_mode, network, workspace, cgo, compiler_directives, target_mode, link_mode, libgcc, package_assembly, host_objects, telemetry and execution_policy. Parse and canonicalize receipt schema 1 and marker schema 2. Keep marker schema 1 readable for schema 1 through 5 installs. Take every golden byte from the caller-supplied rc.5 candidate conformance root under CURATOR_CONFORMANCE_ROOT rather than from a private reimplementation. build-receipt-v2 and install-marker-v3 belong to the go-repository-v1 external-repository line and are out of scope here; the go-v1 compiled-build surface stays receipt v1 plus marker v2. Conformance-claim emission is out of scope and stays with TASK-260720-12r55p, which targets conformance-claim-v3 under rc.5. Do not implement filesystem trust, compiler execution, cache layout, status, or installer mutation.","status":"backlog","title":"Implement canonical build metadata models"}
/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/curator/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260729-v5hqnv/TASK-260729-v5hqnv_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--codex-_RUN-260729-769c54.log:1534:{"ac":"The Python implementation passes the shared rc.5 positive vectors for schema 6, build-root context exclusion, build-source and toolchain bytes, CCJ-1 input and key, canonical receipt and marker, fixed environment and all five Go argv forms, hit and dry-run plans, ordering, commit, rollback, recovery, status, repair, and GC, including all 8 build-drivers.json positive_cases and the byte-exact 11 artifacts under expected/build-driver/ whose cache-key.txt is sha256:529370122ae11e2e961d5265b1a020e046bcd43165b2eb96b05e73a51187ac9b and receipt-sha256.txt is sha256:919fbbad8e6ce95532219fd952c2309d0d7026f85209650508fd6834af4020cd. Named negative coverage includes every minimum cluster from the accepted rc.5 contract: all 77 build-drivers.json rejection_cases, the 10 build_source_cases and 12 toolchain_cases, and from go-host-execution-policy.json the 18 mandatory_controls, the 14 identity_and_protocol_cases, the 8 package_influence_cases, the 11 capability_evidence_cases, the 6 deferred_capability_rejection_guards, and the three failure_boundary outcomes. Execution-policy identity coverage asserts aliases false and three distinct non-alias keys: portable manager-worker-v1 valid, legacy_rc4_without_execution_policy sha256:3fcd714a40e8918eb67dbd35d435875dcce6c9047da811a1fa26626e5e57be48 invalid, and reserved_hardened sha256:13736230d33ce59de7f7323dcd4cffd510655ad8dabd5ee9e8b6cb182ec70037 invalid. Native-control inventory coverage asserts rc5-native-control-inventory-v1 is exhaustive over exactly macos and windows with exactly five controls and the declared per-platform availability and mechanism or reason. Claim coverage asserts claim-version separation across conformance-claim-v1, v2 and v3, that conformance-claim-v3 pins protocol_version 1.0.0-rc.5 and requires build_drivers, and that conformance-claim-v3-qualification.json rules hold: schema-valid-is-not-qualified, driver-platform-subset, no-generic-driver over exactly go-repository-v1 and go-v1, no-unevidenced-platform, linux excluded until TASK-260728-1skseh, and macos and windows pending-downstream-native-evidence. No conformance claim is emitted by this task. Legacy rc.3 vectors remain green. Tests against the exact caller-supplied candidate suite and strict mypy pass, the candidate revision and full manifest digest are recorded as non-release evidence, and no committed curator-spec pin or release claim changes.","blockedBy":["TASK-260720-th0jdi","TASK-260720-3ag6pi","TASK-260729-3nx97g"],"blocks":["TASK-260720-3pemm6","TASK-260720-31zeo2"],"description":"Extend the Python conformance harness as an independent consumer of the protocol 1.0.0-rc.5 schema, build-driver, portable execution-policy, identity, cache, context, and manager-lifecycle vectors.","id":"TASK-260720-12r55p","name":"shared-v6-vector-consumer","notes":"Cross-story release boundary from STORY-260720-21bsr2: consume the candidate suite through the caller-supplied CURATOR_CONFORMANCE_ROOT and leave every committed release pin unchanged. TASK-260720-1utsx8 audits the official pin only after TASK-260720-25d05o qualifies the published protocol release.\nSolution-architecture audit 2026-07-20: scope and AC now distinguish exact candidate-suite consumption through CURATOR_CONFORMANCE_ROOT from the later qualified release-pin change owned solely by TASK-260720-1utsx8.","scope":"Own tests/test_protocol_conformance.py plus focused vector adapters and fixtures that do not duplicate product logic. Consume the exact rc.5 candidate suite through the caller-supplied CURATOR_CONFORMANCE_ROOT, whose manifest.json must hash to sha256:b6f56aacc0e37dcc6692f73f641bff761e89b645adfe20a47a06d81c6fda204c and whose release/1.0.0-rc.5.json records the same required_manifest_sha256; do not edit the committed curator-spec checkout ref in this task. Read every vector and expected artifact from that root; never hard-code a vector input the way Curator internal/godriver/controls_test.go does. Cover generated schema cases for both manifest names, agent-skill-v6 and csk-skill-v6, receipt build-receipt-v1, marker install-marker-v2, conformance-claim-v3, vectors/build-drivers.json, vectors/go-host-execution-policy.json, vectors/conformance-claim-v3-qualification.json, the 11-file expected/build-driver/ tree, and vectors/manager-lifecycle.json. build-receipt-v2, install-marker-v3, schema v7 and the external-repository and registry surfaces belong to the go-repository-v1 line and are out of scope here. The official manager suite pin remains on the previous released protocol until TASK-260720-25d05o qualifies the release and TASK-260720-1utsx8 audits the promotion. Do not import or copy Curator implementation code and do not fabricate release or conformance claims. Retained fail-closed prerequisite: the hard blockedBy edge to TASK-260720-3ag6pi is deliberately kept. TASK-260720-3ag6pi is protocol-v6-conformance-verification, is still status blocked, and is still scoped to the literal rc.4 line, and no rc.5 replacement verification gate exists on the board today, so no relink target was invented. Before this task starts, the Curator-side owner must either retarget TASK-260720-3ag6pi to this rc.5 candidate root and re-review it, or create the rc.5 verification gate and relink this edge to it; resolving that gate is Curator-side work outside this task.","status":"backlog","title":"Consume shared schema v6 vectors"}
/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/curator/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260729-v5hqnv/TASK-260729-v5hqnv_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--codex-_RUN-260729-769c54.log:1536:{"ac":"A valid vendored Go command builds without network under the portable manager-worker-v1 policy, launches only after explicit invocation, receives exact forwarded arguments, returns its exit status, and works through project and global shims on macOS and Windows. Tests prove cache hit without go list or go build, rebuild on source, toolchain, target, execution-policy, receipt or artifact change, no rebuild on irrelevant mode or timestamp change, dry-run byte purity, build-two failure isolation, target-swap rollback, interrupted recovery, identical concurrent publisher handling, and two-project consumer preservation. Native macOS and native Windows jobs run the real fixture across the supported Python matrix with explicit accepted-family Go setup and an exact caller-supplied candidate-suite revision or root whose manifest digest is recorded as non-release evidence. Ubuntu jobs run portable non-driver coverage across the same Python matrix, prove the source-aware go-v1 path fails closed with an unavailable-control error and no worker launch, and neither require nor claim a green go-v1 build; Linux driver success is not asserted anywhere. Per-platform capability evidence matches rc5-native-control-inventory-v1 exactly on each native runner. CI preserves the previous released default pin and has no unexpected skip or xfail. Full relevant pytest and strict mypy pass.","blockedBy":["TASK-260720-12r55p"],"blocks":["TASK-260720-3s27te","TASK-260720-31zeo2","TASK-260728-1e6811"],"description":"Add a minimal real Go skill fixture and end-to-end tests that prove csk can install, cache, activate, launch, repair, and roll back compiled commands on the rc.5 supported platforms, macOS and Windows, while Linux CI keeps portable non-driver coverage only.","id":"TASK-260720-3pemm6","name":"cross-platform-go-build-e2e","notes":"Cross-story release boundary from STORY-260720-21bsr2: cross-platform candidate evidence may use an explicitly supplied suite root, but this task must not commit an unreleased curator-spec ref. Official released-suite pin provenance is audited by TASK-260720-1utsx8 after TASK-260720-25d05o.\nSolution-architecture audit 2026-07-20: scope and AC now keep candidate-suite validation out of the committed release pin. See outcome TASK-260720-3pemm6_release-boundary-plan.md; TASK-260720-1utsx8 alone advances the pin after TASK-260720-25d05o.","scope":"Own new cocoaskills test fixtures, end-to-end and process-level tests, and .github/workflows/ci.yml changes needed to select the operator-trusted accepted Go release family recorded in the protocol and Curator handoff evidence, family 1.25 in the currently accepted Curator implementation with Go 1.23 as the protocol floor only, and to run the exact rc.5 candidate suite without advancing the default committed curator-spec release pin. Real-fixture go-v1 build, cache, activation, launch, repair and rollback coverage runs on native macOS and native Windows runners. The ubuntu jobs keep running portable non-driver coverage such as models, CCJ-1, POSIX cache, locks and transactions, and shims, and must assert that the source-aware go-v1 path fails closed there rather than producing a green build. Cross-platform candidate qualification may accept an explicit immutable curator-spec revision or pre-materialized CURATOR_CONFORMANCE_ROOT as a non-default caller input, and must record its full manifest digest. Exercise project, global, hybrid, mixed script and build commands, and platform shims with real subprocesses. Use injected failures and fake toolchains only for negative paths. Linux go-v1 driver qualification is out of scope and stays with TASK-260728-1skseh and TASK-260728-1e6811. Do not change product semantics except narrowly scoped testability hooks routed to owning tasks; the released-suite pin belongs to TASK-260720-1utsx8 after TASK-260720-25d05o.","status":"backlog","title":"Add cross-platform Go build end-to-end tests"}
